$Module harden 3 "TLS certificate match for SNI; optional client drop"

DESCRIPTION
===========

With multiple TLS certificates, Varnish may fall back to the **last**
one when SNI does not match—so the wrong site can get the wrong cert.
``harden`` stops that: the handshake only succeeds if the certificate
matches the client's SNI (hostname or IP). No SNI or no cert also stops
the handshake.

``harden.close()`` (client context only) closes the client connection
immediately, without sending an HTTP response—similar in idea to nginx
``return 444``.

$Event event
$Function VOID close()
$Restrict client

Force-close the client connection (no HTTP response from this call).
